stripped. The pattern started after `1897911` and persisted
through `9beae2a`.

## Affected files (13 total ‚Äî MUST be re-indented)

All in `synmergia/ui/components/` except bank_npc:

```
boss_health_bar.gd     165 lines
buff_bar.gd            121 lines
combat_log.gd          189 lines
dialog_ui.gd           149 lines
loading_ui.gd          219 lines
minimap.gd             234 lines
name_plate.gd          159 lines
quick_access_bar.gd    135 lines
settings_panel.gd      238 lines
target_frame.gd        221 lines
tooltip_manager.gd     323 lines
world_map.gd           373 lines
synmergia/entities/npcs/bank_npc.gd   29 lines
```

For each of these: `grep -cP '^\t' file.gd` returns **0**.

The non-broken siblings (good reference for the expected
format): `action_bar.gd`, `bank_ui.gd`, `character_panel.gd`,
`chat_ui.gd`, `menu_manager.gd`, `quest_ui.gd`,
`input_manager.gd`, `vault_service.gd`, `quest_service.gd`.

## Root cause (working hypothesis)

The file-edit tool the previous session used appears to have
**stripped leading whitespace on multi-line writes**. Single
line edits were unaffected (the `8640b09` modernization commit
touched existing files via targeted edits and they kept their
tabs). The problem only shows up in the new files created in
`create` mode. Test on a single file before doing bulk fixes.

## Static checks (this session, no Godot available)

- ‚úÖ Braces balanced in all 13 broken files
- ‚úÖ Parens balanced in all 13
- ‚úÖ Brackets balanced in all 13
- ‚úÖ `func` (not `def`) used everywhere
- ‚úÖ No mixed tabs/spaces in broken files (everything is just
     all-spaces with zero indent)
- ‚ùå Zero leading tabs in 13 files ‚Äî **blocker**

The structural code looks correct. The fix is mechanical: add
indentation.

